his TM. It contains my favorite move, Steel Wing."#If you don't mind me asking...":How does looking at this ancient mural make you feel?"(Yes, it's very impressive isn't it?"nThe fact that ancient people could draw such a beautiful mural that has stood the test of time like this."�The creature that is depicted in this mural appears to be a fusion between an \C[2]earth titan \C[0] and a \C[1]water titan\C[0]."_Yes, the creature that is depicted in this mural appears to have wielded tremendous power."eIt probably stroke fear in the hearts of the people that lived back then if it really did exist."]It appears to be a fusion between an \C[2]earth titan \C[0] and a \C[1]water titan\C[0]." I share this sentiment too."�DNA Splicers are new technology. So how could a mural that was painted thousands of years ago depict what seems to be a Pokémon fusion?"QHah! Not everyone has an interest for ancient history, that's quite alright!".Still, I find it to be quite fascinating."�The creature that is depicted in this mural appears to be a fusion between an \C[2]earth titan \C[0]and a \C[1]water titan\C[0]."�They say that long ago, an \C[3]asteroid\C[0] that crashed into the Earth carried a special gene that spread to all living Pokémon."bThat gene gave Pokémon the ability to fuse together, long before DNA Splicers were invented."\It lies dormant within every Pokémon today. DNA Splicers work by forcing it to awaken."~This is how this creature, along with every natural Pokémon fusion came to be... At least, that's what scientists think."�You know, my father, the president of Devon Corp., recently discovered a rare stone that emits strong fusion energy while drilling near Sootopolis City."YNo one knows for sure, but we think it could be a shard from that original asteroid."nThis mural lends credence to the theory, don't you think? That's why I wanted to see it with my own eyes."�To my father, this meteorite is just a way to manufacture DNA Splicers for cheap. But I think the im